USER ```
USER # CONVENTIONS — Aider Session Rules (token_effectivenes project)
USER # Loaded as read-only cached context. ~1200 tokens. Do not remove.
USER 
USER ## WORKFLOW (mandatory for all non-trivial changes)
USER - Non-trivial = changes behavior, touches >1 file, touches deps/config/schema
USER - Preflight before ANY implementation: research → spec → task triad must exist
USER - Triad: docs/research/<feature>.html + docs/specs/<feature>_spec.html + tasks/active/<task>.html
USER - Exception: single-file typo/comment fixes only
USER - Each spec step: changes ONE thing, tests ONE thing, proves ONE thing
USER - If a step description has "and" → split it into two steps
USER 
USER ## ATOMIC DECOMPOSITION
USER - A task > ~2 hours of focused work → too big, split it
USER - Implement one atomic step → test → mark done → move to next
USER - Never start step N+1 before step N exit condition passes
USER 
USER ## WRITE-GATE (critical)
USER - A decision is NOT real until it exists in a file, in the SAME TURN as approval
USER - Forbidden: "great, I'll do that" → [session ends] → LOST
USER - After any approval: write the file, confirm "written to [file]"
USER 
USER ## MEMORY PROTOCOL
USER - Single-Owner Rule: each fact lives in exactly ONE canonical file, others link to it
USER   - Project metrics/counts → memories/repo/project_structure.md
USER   - Session history → docs/memory/checkpoint_YYYY-MM-DD.md (immutable after session)
USER   - Roadmap/phase order → active task file
USER   - Architecture decisions → docs/adr/
USER - Checkpoint every session end — no exceptions, agent writes it proactively
USER - Cold-start: read AGENT_INDEX.md → project_structure.md → latest checkpoint → active tasks
USER 
USER ## DEBUGGING (hard rules)
USER - Two-Failed-Attempt Rule: after 2 unsuccessful fixes on same problem → STOP patching
USER - Switch to: reproduce → instrument → hypothesize → verify → fix → regress
USER - Before any edit state: "Bug is at [location] because [reason]. Disconfirmed by: [check]"
USER 
USER ## SECURITY CHECKLIST (before any production code)
USER - No injection (SQL, shell, template)
USER - No hardcoded secrets — all keys in .env
USER - Input validation at system boundaries
USER - Sensitive data not logged
USER - Error messages don't leak internals
USER 
USER ## TOKEN EFFICIENCY RULES (this project)
USER - Always use --cache-prompts (already in .aider.conf.yml)
USER - Only /add files you will actually edit this session — drop when done
USER - Use /read-only for reference files (cheaper, cached separately)
USER - Prefer diffs over full rewrites in responses
USER - Don't ask Claude to "explain reasoning" unless debugging
USER - Weak model (haiku) handles: commits, summarization, simple Q&A
USER - Sonnet for: architecture, complex logic, multi-file changes
USER - Run `python scripts/prewarm_cache.py` at session start
USER 
USER ## INTERNET RESEARCH (mandatory before using any external library/API)
USER 1. Known URL → fetch directly (free)
USER 2. Unknown URL → search first
USER 3. Never assert API signatures, endpoints, or params from memory — always verify
USER 4. Mark unverified facts as UNVERIFIED explicitly
USER 
USER ## PROJECT STRUCTURE
USER - Research: docs/research/  |  Specs: docs/specs/  |  Tasks: tasks/active/
USER - Memory: docs/memory/ (checkpoints)  |  Repo facts: memories/repo/project_structure.md
USER - Scripts: scripts/  |  Wiki: wiki/  |  Protocols: protocols/
USER 
USER ## IMPLEMENTATION DISCIPLINE
USER - Only make changes directly requested or clearly necessary
USER - Don't add docstrings/comments/type annotations to code you didn't change
USER - Don't add error handling for scenarios that can't happen
USER - Don't create helpers or abstractions for one-time operations
USER - Don't refactor, add features, or "improve" beyond what was asked
USER - Read a file before modifying it — understand existing code first
USER - After editing: run tests or exit-condition check immediately
USER 
USER ## CODE QUALITY GATES (before marking any step done)
USER - All tests pass: pytest (or equivalent)
USER - Lint clean: ruff check (Python)
USER - No hardcoded secrets anywhere in diff
USER - Exit condition from spec explicitly verified (not just "looks right")
USER - Checkpoint written if end of session
USER 
USER ## GIT DISCIPLINE
USER - `git status` / `git diff` before any commit — read-only, always safe
USER - Never `git push --force`, `git reset --hard`, or `rm -rf` without user confirmation
USER - Commit messages: imperative mood, reference task step (e.g. "Add .aider.conf.yml [step 1.3]")
USER - Never amend published commits
USER 
USER ## MATH / ESTIMATION WORK
USER - Define the quantity being estimated before writing any formula
USER - State assumptions explicitly
USER - Name numerical stability concerns
USER - Anchor to a trusted source (paper, library docs) — never assert from memory
USER - Present implementation options before locking in
USER 
USER ## AIDER-SPECIFIC WORKFLOW
USER - Start session: `python scripts/prewarm_cache.py` → then `aider` (or `make dev`)
USER - In Aider chat: `/add <file>` only files you will edit this session
USER - When done with a file: `/drop <file>` to remove from context
USER - Reference files: `/read-only <file>` — cheaper, cached separately
USER - Check cache stats: run with `--no-stream` and read usage block in .aider.llm.history
USER - After session: `python scripts/token_report.py` to see cost breakdown
USER - If Aider suggests wrong edit: `/undo` then rephrase more specifically
USER 
USER ## ANTHROPIC API NOTES (verified 2026-05-13)
USER - Model IDs: claude-sonnet-4-5, claude-haiku-3-5, claude-haiku-4-5, claude-opus-4-5
USER - Cache minimum: 1024 tokens for claude-sonnet-4-5
USER - Cache TTL default: 5 minutes (refreshed free on hit)
USER - Cache read cost: 10% of base input price
USER - Output tokens: 5x more expensive than input — keep responses concise
USER - Batch API: 50% discount, async (up to 24h), good for non-interactive work
USER 
USER ## MODEL ROUTING (5 tiers — verified 2026-05-13)
USER Env keys for all backbone providers: see `.env.example` (copy to `.env`). LiteLLM list: https://aider.chat/docs/llms/other.html
USER Full decision matrix: docs/research/model_tiering.html
USER - T1 FREE:  gemini/gemini-2.5-flash (free tier, 44% polyglot) — explain/read only
USER - T2 CHEAP: deepseek/deepseek-chat ($0.14/MTok in, 70% polyglot) ← DEFAULT for coding
USER - T3 MID:   deepseek/deepseek-reasoner ($0.14/MTok, thinking mode, 74% polyglot)
USER             gemini/gemini-2.5-flash ($0.30/MTok, fast)
USER - T4 MAIN:  gemini/gemini-2.5-pro ($1.25/MTok, 79-83% polyglot, free tier)
USER             claude-sonnet-4-5 ($3/MTok, use when caching pays off or AWOS artifacts)
USER - T5 HEAVY: claude-opus-4-5 ($5 in / $25 out per MTok — see memories/repo/models_pricing_catalog.md) — only after T4 fails
USER 
USER ESCALATE when: T2 fails twice, multi-file architecture, AWOS artifact creation
USER STAY at T2 for: bug fixes, tests, refactoring, feature impl from spec
USER Makefile: make dev-cheap (T2), make dev-think (T3), make dev-mid (T3), make dev-pro (T4), make dev (T4 Sonnet)
USER ```
